					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/chazzk" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1203158); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1203158&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973921" alt="ChazzK" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1203158)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/chazzk" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1203158); return false;" >ChazzK</a></span> <span class="odate time_1344349297 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Aug 2012 14:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1530130">
									

<p>I've definitely got a feeling of the start (to the main part) of 28 Days Later here. Or maybe the last part of the first Resident Evil movie.</p>
<p>I think something that was a little overly subtle was the fact that Catherine woke up, and the <em>entire hospital ward</em> she was in was empty and half-dark. That only happens during an evacuation or when the hospital is closed down for one reason or another; neither a situation (normally) where someone would be left behind.</p>
<p>Also the fact that the bandages had been on so long that they *hardened to the point that they shattered* when she moved, and when she got up her wounds were at least mostly healed over, if not fully/internally healed.</p>
<p>Catherine was asleep a long while. Something very bad happened in the &quot;hospital&quot; where she was at during that time.</p>
<p>I'm aching for a part 2.</p>

							</div>

								
					
